A cricket contains more protein than most people expect. It also contains everything required to make most people

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:13,000
stop chewing. Six legs, two antenna, large eyes, and the unmistakable appearance of something that should be

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:22,000
removed from the kitchen, not seasoned inside it. This creates a strange contradiction. Humans eat cows, pigs,

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:30,000
chickens, fish, crabs, shrimp, snails, frogs, octopuses, sea urchins, and animals whose internal organs are

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,000
considered delicacies. We grind bones into gelatin. We ferment milk until it

6
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:45,000
smells suspicious. We allow mold to grow through cheese and then charge more for it. But place one roasted grasshopper

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,000
beside dinner and suddenly everyone becomes extremely concerned about dignity. The obvious explanation is

8
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:58,000
disgust. Insects look dirty. They crawl through garbage. Some bite, sting,

9
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:06,000
spread disease, destroy crops, invade homes, and appear unexpectedly in bathrooms during vulnerable moments. Of

10
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:13,000
course, we do not eat them. Except humans do. People consume thousands of insect species across Africa, Asia,

11
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Latin America, Oceanania, and parts of North America. Beetles, caterpillars, ants, termites, grasshoppers, crickets,

12
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:30,000
wasps, bees, cicas, and true bugs have all become food. Not emergency food, not

13
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:39,000
punishment food, actual food. Some are roasted until crisp. Others are boiled, fried, smoked, ground into sauces, mixed

14
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:47,000
with spices, wrapped in leaves, added to stews, or eaten as expensive seasonal delicacies. In parts of southern Africa,

15
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:54,000
mopane caterpillars support major regional trade. In Thailand, farmed crickets appear in markets and packaged

16
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:03,000
snacks. In Mexico, chapulines are toasted with salt, lime, garlic, or chili. Ant eggs can become a prized

17
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:11,000
ingredient rather than evidence that the pantry has surrendered. So the question is not really why humans do not eat insects. The question is why some humans

18
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:18,000
stopped seeing them as food. And protein alone cannot answer it. A food can be nutritious, efficient, abundant, and

19
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:23,000
environmentally promising yet still fail the most important test in human eating.

20
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:29,000
It must feel edible. That feeling begins long before food reaches the mouth.

21
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Imagine two plates. One contains a small pink animal with a curved body, armored shell, black eyes, numerous legs, and

22
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:45,000
long antenna. The other contains a shrimp. They are the same plate. Yet shrimp often feels elegant, while a cricket feels like a home inspection

23
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:53,000
problem. Biologically, both are arthropods. Both wear skeletons on the outside. Both must be cooked and peeled

24
00:02:53,000 --> 00:03:00,000
or processed correctly. Both can trigger allergies. Both have bodies that would look deeply questionable if culture had

25
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:08,000
not spent generations teaching us the correct emotional response. The shrimp did not earn respect through appearance.

26
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,000
It received excellent public relations.

27
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:20,000
That is the first key. Humans do not judge food by nutrition alone. We judge it through categories learned in childhood. A chicken belongs in the food

28
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:27,000
category. A cockroach belongs in the contamination category. Once the brain places an animal into one of those

29
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:37,000
boxes, moving it becomes remarkably difficult. A child does not calculate amino acid profiles before accepting a chicken nugget. The surrounding culture

30
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:44,000
has already completed the difficult work. It selected the species, raised it away from view, removed the feathers,

31
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:55,000
feet, blood, organs, head, and recognizable body shape, ground the remaining tissue, coated it in crumbs, and served it beside.

32
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:59,000
By the time the child sees the chicken, the chicken has become geometry.

33
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Insects usually arrive with their biography intact. The legs remain attached. The eyes are visible. The

34
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,000
wings announce what the animal used to do.

35
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:19,000
The entire body says, "You know exactly what this is." That matters because visible animal features activate disgust more strongly than anonymous protein.

36
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Many meat eaters prefer cuts that do not resemble the animal. A steak is easier to categorize as food than a cow's face.

37
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:36,000
A fish fillet is easier than a fish watching from the plate. A sausage is meat with the evidence professionally removed. A whole roasted cricket offers

38
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:43,000
no such emotional assistance. It is honest to a fault. But disgust is not simply irrational weakness. It evolved

39
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:52,000
partly as protection. Humans need to avoid pathogens, parasites, toxins, spoiled food, feces, and decomposing

40
00:04:52,000 --> 00:05:01,000
material. The disgust system helps by creating fast rejection before slow reasoning can begin. Bad smells, unusual

41
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:14,000
textures, bodily fluids, crawling movement, and signs of contamination can trigger an immediate response. This system is useful. It is also imprecise.

42
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:21,000
Disgust does not operate like a laboratory. It operates like an overly nervous security guard. If something

43
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:25,000
resembles a threat, it may be rejected before identification.

44
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:33,000
Insects frequently appear near exactly the materials humans should avoid. Flies visit waste and carcasses. Cockroaches

45
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:42,000
move through drains and garbage. Beetles emerge from stored food. Maggots appear in decay. Mosquitoes arrive for blood.

46
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:50,000
Termites eat buildings. Ants locate sugar approximately 4 seconds after it becomes unguarded. Even harmless insects

47
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:59,000
become associated with infestation. A single insect in a restaurant can suggest poor sanitation because diners reasonably wonder what else is moving

48
